/**
 * Every gameplay constant, with its unit (ARCHITECTURE rule 6). Lead-owned.
 *
 * Wave 1 agents: if you need a new constant, add it to a `const LOCAL_TUNING = { ... }` block at the
 * top of your own file with the change-request marker of docs/briefs/_COMMON.md and list it in your report. The lead
 * moves it here between waves. Do not edit this file directly.
 *
 * [TUN-1] Every sim / AI module block (the former LOCAL_TUNING / *_TUNING blocks) now lives at the end of this file, one
 * block per module (T_FLIGHT ... T_DEFENDING, grouped sim ball / players / kicks / defend / control / keeper / rules,
 * then AI); the modules import them. Old location -> new name: docs/TUNING.md "TUN-1".
 *
 * [TUN-2] The formerly inline sim / AI gameplay literals were added to their module's block (each marked [TUN-2]; new
 * blocks T_QUERY and T_SETPIECE_SPOTS, the set-piece spot templates, after T_SETPIECE_AI); the input, modes and
 * formation-remap blocks are at the end of the file (T_TOUCH_STICK ... T_FORMATION_REMAP). Non-gameplay modules
 * (render, audio, ui, net, platform, app, data generation) keep their values in a local block marked
 * `// LOCAL_TUNING (non-gameplay: <reason>)`. Old location -> new name: docs/TUNING.md "TUN-2".
 *
 * Values are starting points derived from section 6 reference feel; FIX-14 tunes them.
 */
